ce mapping records a Lean statement that implies the printed one. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.lem-dyadic-excess-reformulation"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.lem-dyadic-excess-reformulation"],"id":"long.lem-dyadic-excess-reformulation","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Lemma 6.54 (An integer test for the interval between the dyadic and Mersenne weights)","locator":"Long record Lemma 6.54, p. 59, label lem:dyadic-excess-reformulation","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*For positive integers $p,L$ and $n\\ge0$, write the residual as $p/(2L)$ and put $E=2^np-L$. Clearing positive denominators gives\n$$\n\\frac{p}{2L}\\le\\frac1{2^{n+1}}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad E\\le0,\n \\qquad\n \\frac1{2^{n+1}}<\\frac{p}{2L}<\\frac1{2^{n+1}-1}\n \\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad 0<E<\\frac p2.\n$$\nThe first test concerns the dyadic bound, not the greedy selection threshold itself. The second identifies precisely the interval in which a Mersenne weight is skipped but the dyadic safety test fails.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.lem-dyadic-excess-reformulation","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.lem-dyadic-excess-reformulation","id":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.lem-dyadic-excess-reformulation%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.divInt_le_nextDyadic_iff_excess_nonpos%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.lem-dyadic-excess-reformulation%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.divInt_le_nextDyadic_iff_excess_nonpos%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/lean.Erd